  "description": "(T1) Sycamore  - Lateral crown reduction. The tree is approximately 16m in height. No reduction of height proposed.\rReduce western lateral spread by 2m from 11m to 9m. Reduction to shape canopy, pruning to suitable points and maintaining natural aesthetic. Work undertaken to cut back the canopy over the neighbours roof to allow 2m gap as the branches now hit the structure. \rSycamore (T2) -Crown lift. The tree is approximately 16m in height. There is no reduction of height proposed. Remove the lowest limb. Will reduce the lowest portion of crown by 5m from 11m to 6m. Reduction to shape canopy, pruning to suitable points and maintaining natural aesthetic.\rWork undertaken to improve light conditions in the neighbouring garden. The tree will tolerate the pruning as specified above.",
